  "Question": "Suppose that \\(4^a = 5,\\) \\(5^b = 6,\\) \\(6^c = 7,\\) and \\(7^d = 8.\\) What is \\(a \\cdot b \\cdot c \\cdot d?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac32\\)",
    "C": "\\(2\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac52\\)",
    "E": "\\(3\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The result of each power is the base in the next equation. Raising successively to the next exponent therefore combines all four equations. Since every base is positive, the power-of-a-power law gives\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n4^{ab}&=(4^a)^b=5^b=6,\\\\\n4^{abc}&=(4^{ab})^c=6^c=7,\\\\\n4^{abcd}&=(4^{abc})^d=7^d=8.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nNow \\(4=2^2\\) and \\(8=2^3\\), so\n\\[\n2^{2abcd}=2^3.\n\\]\nPowers of \\(2\\) increase strictly with their exponents, so equal powers have equal exponents. Thus \\(2abcd=3\\), giving \\(abcd=\\frac32\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
